  "notes": "{諦|あきら}める means to give up on something, accepting that it cannot be achieved or obtained. It implies resignation rather than simply stopping.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Takes ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧: ⟦{夢|ゆめ}→夢：01519_yume⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{諦|あきら}める (to give up on a dream)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{諦|あきら}めて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means \"have given up\" — the state of having resigned oneself.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{諦|あきら}める: to give up on ~\n- {諦|あきら}めず⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧: without giving up\n- ⟦{諦|あきら}め→諦め：07166_akirame⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{悪|わる}い→悪い：00908_warui⟧: reluctant to give up, won't take no for an answer\n- ⟦{諦|あきら}め→諦め：07166_akirame⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦つく→付く：01960_tsuku⟧: to come to terms with giving up\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{断念|だんねん}する→断念する：20717_dannensuru⟧: to give up, to abandon a plan (formal, often used for decisions)\n- ⟦やめる→やめる：00909_yameru⟧: to stop, to quit (more neutral, less emotional)\n- ⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{引|ひ}く→引く：01978_hiku⟧: to withdraw, to pull out (of a project or venture)",
